True, but alt.* has been hoist upon its own petard of chaos.

The alt.* hiearachy is a cross-section; you can find everything from
binaries to sources to sympathy, all of which are created "on the fly."

If a site were to automatically accept newgroups in the alt.* hierarchy,
they would pick up a ton of baggage (which might be) inconsistent with 
their policies.  If, on the other hand, they go through the newgroup
messages by hand, they're open to charges of censorship.

For many sites, the headache of either choice isn't worth it; as a
result, they don't carry alt.*, and I don't blame them.

I've suggested (many times, it seems) that alt.comp.acad-freedom.*
doesn't belong in alt.*; it would get much better distribution as
either a comp.* or soc.* newsgroup.  The last response I saw was
that "it isn't worth the time to run a Call for Votes."  (Inciden-
tally, I would *vociferously* support a proposal for something like
comp.acad-freedom.talk/comp.acad-freedom.news; they belong in a more
widespread hierarchy.) 

>(Nor does it hold for Bitnet Listservers, where the Usenet gate puts
>them all under bit.listserv.* regardless of content, etc.)

I wasn't aware that BITNET lists were automatically gatewayed; I thought
that bit.listserv.* newsgroups had to go through the new group process as
well...

