The _size_ of the post matters. If he'd restricted it to just "Jesus is
coming." (one letter less than "Have a nice day."), he'd have been
flamed a LOT less. (The followups would have been somewhat more ribald,
though :-) "Just hit `n'" may be good advice but long off topic posts are
a bit like auto wrecks - you've just got to read to the end, then you get
annoyed that you did, then you flame the guy who posted the article for
wasting your time. Illogical, but very human. In this case he _wanted_
everyone to read it, so presumably went to some effort to catch people's
eye. The opening `doom and disaster' paragraph was a bit like a tabloid
headline.

