Normally Canada is a liberal democracy with little censorship. The problem
is that Internet and related networks are a new medium. Conservative
minded sysop adminstrators, especially at universities, are pulling out
their electronic scissors and snipping possibly offensive bits in fear they
may lose public support (a funding) or be bagged by the police. 
 
Canada is a little less absolute in the application of rights compared to
the US. Our Charter of Rights (article 1) says its okay to step on
individual rights if it is for the collective good (not the exact
wording). This setsthe tone being used by the sysops. 

In time, our culture will adjust to this new medium and we should see less
knee-jerk reactions.  I hope!

